Subject: [PATCH] Exhaust individual backhaul candidates before scanning again

An autonomous reconnect can see an unrooted former parent and a working root
at the same RSSI. The connect timeout discarded the entire scan after the
global retry budget, before trying the next candidate. The next scan reset
every per-candidate counter and selected the same former parent indefinitely.

Keep the scan snapshot on a scan-list connection timeout. ext_try_connecting
already bounds each candidate with STA_MAX_CONNECT_ATTEMPT and requests a new
scan once no candidate remains. Explicit new-parent/last-parent transactions
retain their existing global deadline and fallback. Do not change admission,
RSSI preference, retry intervals, or retry limits.

Upstream-Status: Pending

--- a/source/core/services/vap_svc_mesh_ext.c
+++ b/source/core/services/vap_svc_mesh_ext.c
@@ -525,6 +525,12 @@
         return 0;
     }
 
+    if (ext->conn_state == connection_state_connection_in_progress) {
+        ext->conn_retry = 0;
+        schedule_connect_sm(svc);
+        return 0;
+    }
+
     if (ext->conn_retry >= STA_MAX_CONNECT_ATTEMPT) {
         wifi_util_error_print(WIFI_CTRL, "%s:%d not received connection event\n", __func__,
             __LINE__);
